      "text": "## Mineral Classification by Anion"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#006",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mineralogy:00-overview, git-history:mineralogy:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "mineralogy/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "mineralogy/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:mineralogy:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mineralogy",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "mineralogy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Mineralogy - Overview and Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nMINERAL CLASSES (by dominant anion group)\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                                                  |\n|  SILICATES          ~1,000 species       Rock-forming backbone   |\n|  SiO₄ tetrahedra    Quartz, feldspar, mica, pyroxene, olivine    |\n|                                                                  |\n|  CARBONATES           ~200 species       Sedimentary record      |\n|  CO₃²⁻              Calcite, dolomite, aragonite, malachite      |\n|                                                                  |\n|  OXIDES               ~500 species       Economic ores           |\n|  O²⁻                 Hematite, magnetite, corundum, rutile       |\n|                                                                  |\n|  SULFIDES             ~600 species       Ore minerals            |\n|  S²⁻                 Pyrite, galena, sphalerite, chalcopyrite    |\n|                                                                  |\n|  PHOSPHATES           ~700 species       Bones, fertilizer       |\n|  PO₄³⁻               Apatite, turquoise, monazite                |\n|                                                                  |\n|  SULFATES             ~400 species       Evaporites              |\n|  SO₄²⁻               Gypsum, barite, celestite                   |\n|                                                                  |\n|  HALIDES              ~100 species       Evaporites, fluxes      |\n|  F⁻, Cl⁻             Halite, fluorite, sylvite                   |\n|                                                                  |\n|  NATIVE ELEMENTS       ~50 species       Pure metals/metalloids  |\n|                        Gold, silver, copper, diamond, graphite   |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
