      "text": "## Mineral vs. Rock vs. Crystal"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#009",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mineralogy:00-overview, git-history:mineralogy:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "mineralogy/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "mineralogy/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:mineralogy:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mineralogy",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "mineralogy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Mineralogy - Overview and Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "| Property | Mineral | Rock | Crystal |\n|----------|---------|------|---------|\n| **Chemical composition** | Fixed or narrow range | Variable aggregate | Same as parent mineral |\n| **Crystalline structure** | Always | Usually amorphous mix | Well-developed external faces |\n| **Example** | Quartz (SiO₂) | Quartzite (mostly quartz) | Quartz crystal (hexagonal prism) |\n| **Named by** | IMA | Petrologists | Crystallographers |"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#010",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mineralogy:00-overview, git-history:mineralogy:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "mineralogy/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "mineralogy/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:mineralogy:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mineralogy",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "mineralogy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Mineralogy - Overview and Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Mineroids**: naturally occurring solids that fail one mineral criterion. Opal (amorphous), obsidian (volcanic glass), amber (organic), coal (organic/amorphous) — often called minerals colloquially, technically are not."
    },
