      "text": "## Crystal Systems in Brief"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#017",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mineralogy:00-overview, git-history:mineralogy:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "mineralogy/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "mineralogy/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:mineralogy:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mineralogy",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "mineralogy",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Mineralogy - Overview and Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nSEVEN CRYSTAL SYSTEMS\n+--------------------------------------------------------+\n|  System        | Axes / Angles          | Examples     |\n+--------------------------------------------------------+\n|  Cubic         | a=b=c; 90°,90°,90°     | Halite, gold |\n|  Tetragonal    | a=b≠c; 90°,90°,90°     | Zircon       |\n|  Orthorhombic  | a≠b≠c; 90°,90°,90°     | Olivine      |\n|  Hexagonal     | a=b≠c; 90°,90°,120°    | Quartz       |\n|  Trigonal      | a=b=c; α=β=γ≠90°       | Calcite      |\n|  Monoclinic    | a≠b≠c; 90°,β,90°       | Feldspar     |\n|  Triclinic     | a≠b≠c; α≠β≠γ≠90°       | Kyanite      |\n+--------------------------------------------------------+\n  32 crystallographic point groups\n  230 space groups (the complete symmetry classification)\n  → Direct application of finite group theory to 3D geometry\n```"
    },
